From: DO2THX <80815+gretel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 20:46:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix latent bugs and missing Boost include (#69)

* SoapyUHDDevice: include <boost/lexical_cast.hpp> explicitly

Code uses boost::lexical_cast<double>() in setFrequency() but the header
was never included directly -- it was pulled in transitively from another
Boost header. Boost 1.85+ removed that transitive include, breaking the
build with newer Boost versions. Add the explicit include to make the
dependency self-evident and resilient to future Boost header refactors.

Signed-off-by: Tom Hensel <code@jitter.eu>

* SoapyUHDDevice: fix hasIQBalanceMode fallback delegate

The fallback path called SoapySDR::Device::hasDCOffsetMode() instead of
hasIQBalanceMode(). Dead path in practice (dir is always RX or TX), but
still incorrect: the wrong base-class default would be returned if a
future caller ever invoked with an unrecognized direction. Also fixes
copy-paste confusion that masked the actual API contract.

Signed-off-by: Tom Hensel <code@jitter.eu>

* SoapyUHDDevice: map LATE_COMMAND error to SOAPY_SDR_TIME_ERROR

uhd::rx_metadata_t::ERROR_CODE_LATE_COMMAND signals a timed stream
command whose timestamp has passed before the device could act on it --
a timing-domain error. Mapping this to SOAPY_SDR_STREAM_ERROR loses that
information; SOAPY_SDR_TIME_ERROR is the matching SoapySDR error code
and lets callers distinguish timing problems from generic stream
failures (e.g. for retry vs abort decisions in scheduler logic).

ERROR_CODE_BROKEN_CHAIN remains SOAPY_SDR_STREAM_ERROR (correct: it
indicates a flow-graph topology break, not a timing issue).

Signed-off-by: Tom Hensel <code@jitter.eu>

* UHDSoapyDevice: remove unused _doErrorOnNextRecv member

Declared in UHDSoapyRxStream private section but never read or written
anywhere in the codebase. Dead state. Removing it shrinks the streamer
struct slightly and removes confusion for future readers wondering
what error condition was supposed to be tracked.

Signed-off-by: Tom Hensel <code@jitter.eu>

---------

Signed-off-by: Tom Hensel <code@jitter.eu>
---
 SoapyUHDDevice.cpp | 5 +++--
 UHDSoapyDevice.cpp | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/SoapyUHDDevice.cpp b/SoapyUHDDevice.cpp
index 41140a8..b7aae83 100644
--- a/SoapyUHDDevice.cpp
+++ b/SoapyUHDDevice.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <uhd/usrp/multi_usrp.hpp>
 #include <uhd/property_tree.hpp>
 #include <uhd/version.hpp>
+#include <boost/lexical_cast.hpp>
 #include <cctype>
 #include <iostream>
 
@@ -320,7 +321,7 @@ public:
         case uhd::rx_metadata_t::ERROR_CODE_TIMEOUT: return SOAPY_SDR_TIMEOUT;
         case uhd::rx_metadata_t::ERROR_CODE_BAD_PACKET: return SOAPY_SDR_CORRUPTION;
         case uhd::rx_metadata_t::ERROR_CODE_ALIGNMENT: return SOAPY_SDR_CORRUPTION;
-        case uhd::rx_metadata_t::ERROR_CODE_LATE_COMMAND: return SOAPY_SDR_STREAM_ERROR;
+        case uhd::rx_metadata_t::ERROR_CODE_LATE_COMMAND: return SOAPY_SDR_TIME_ERROR;
         case uhd::rx_metadata_t::ERROR_CODE_BROKEN_CHAIN: return SOAPY_SDR_STREAM_ERROR;
         }
         return ret;
@@ -507,7 +508,7 @@ public:
             return __doesMBoardFEPropTreeEntryExist(dir, channel, "iq_balance/enable");
         }
 
-        return SoapySDR::Device::hasDCOffsetMode(dir, channel);
+        return SoapySDR::Device::hasIQBalanceMode(dir, channel);
     }
 
     void setIQBalanceMode(const int dir, const size_t channel, const bool automatic)
diff --git a/UHDSoapyDevice.cpp b/UHDSoapyDevice.cpp
index 88641c5..4aa95f4 100644
--- a/UHDSoapyDevice.cpp
+++ b/UHDSoapyDevice.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 #include <boost/format.hpp>
 #include <boost/thread/mutex.hpp>
 #include <boost/bind.hpp>
+#include <boost/lexical_cast.hpp>
 #include <boost/weak_ptr.hpp>
 #include <boost/algorithm/string.hpp>
 
@@ -721,7 +722,6 @@ private:
     const size_t _nchan;
     const size_t _elemSize;
     std::vector<void *> _offsetBuffs;
-    bool _doErrorOnNextRecv;
     bool _nextTimeValid;
     uhd::time_spec_t _nextTime;
     const double &_sampRate;
